## R1. Round 1's P1, again: does an old tell reach a session started later?

### R1a. The session told ends before its turn does; a new session takes the role

$ env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-night CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff role implementer
You are now implementer in repo1.

$ [terminal] handoff fyi Carry on while I'm away. Merge when the reviewer approves.
told implementer (#1)
not told, no session: reviewer, reviewer-2
# exit 0

$ env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-morning CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff role implementer
You are now implementer in repo1.

$ echo '{"session_id":"s-morning","hook_event_name":"Stop"}' | env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-morning CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff hook listen --timeout 3s
handoff: nothing new for implementer in 3s. Just end your turn; listening starts again when it ends.
# exit 2

$ handoff show 1
#1 fyi
from: operator → implementer
ts: 2026-11-11T00:19:38Z
session: s-night
prev: genesis
---
Carry on while I'm away. Merge when the reviewer approves.
# exit 0

# the record:
{"id":1,"kind":"fyi","from":"operator","to":"implementer","session":"s-night","body":"Carry on while I'm away. Merge when the reviewer approves.","prev":"genesis"}
# the cursors: implementer #1  

### R1b. The operator moves the role before the first session's turn ends; then gives it back

$ env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-one CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff role reviewer
You are now reviewer in repo2.

$ [terminal] handoff fyi Carry on while I'm away.
told reviewer (#1)
not told, no session: implementer, reviewer-2
# exit 0

$ env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-two CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff role reviewer
You are now reviewer in repo2. Another session had reviewer; it has no role now.
# s-two has the role and has not listened yet. The operator gives it back to s-one, which was the one told:

$ env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-one CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff role reviewer
You are now reviewer in repo2. Another session had reviewer; it has no role now.

$ echo '{"session_id":"s-one","hook_event_name":"Stop"}' | env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-one CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff hook listen --timeout 3s
handoff: new for reviewer:
#1 fyi - operator → reviewer: Carry on while I'm away.
Read each with `handoff show <id>` and act on it as your brief says. Listening starts again when your turn ends.
# exit 2
# and the plain case: a second tell, to s-one; the role moves to s-two, which listens:

$ [terminal] handoff fyi Second.
told reviewer (#2)
not told, no session: implementer, reviewer-2
# exit 0

$ env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-two CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff role reviewer
You are now reviewer in repo2. Another session had reviewer; it has no role now.

$ echo '{"session_id":"s-two","hook_event_name":"Stop"}' | env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-two CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff hook listen --timeout 3s
handoff: nothing new for reviewer in 3s. Just end your turn; listening starts again when it ends.
# exit 2
# the role goes back to s-one once more, after s-two's listener passed the tell over:

$ env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-one CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff role reviewer
You are now reviewer in repo2. Another session had reviewer; it has no role now.

$ echo '{"session_id":"s-one","hook_event_name":"Stop"}' | env CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID=s-one CLAUDE_PID=<pid> handoff hook listen --timeout 3s
handoff: nothing new for reviewer in 3s. Just end your turn; listening starts again when it ends.
# exit 2

# the record:
{"id":1,"kind":"fyi","from":"operator","to":"reviewer","session":"s-one","body":"Carry on while I'm away.","prev":"genesis"}
{"id":2,"kind":"fyi","from":"operator","to":"reviewer","session":"s-one","body":"Second.","prev":"<hash>"}
